        "original_id": "410e8782-eb41-56fb-8225-6fc17582c62c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Angell, Harry Stephen Keeler\n- Products: Season Ticket: A Baseball Companion, Five Seasons, Late Innings, The Summer Game, The Strange Adventure of the Twelve Coins of Confucius, Sing Sing Nights, The Mysterious Mr. Wong\n- Organizations: The New Yorker\n- Topics: American writing, sports writing, baseball, mystery fiction, science fiction\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Stephen Keeler was born on November 3, 1890, and he became a prolific but little-known American author of mysteries and science fiction.\n- Roger Angell was born on September 19, 1920, and he is an American essayist known for writing about sports, especially baseball.\n- Harry Stephen Keeler wrote the 1928 short story \"The Strange Adventure of the Twelve Coins of Confucius,\" which was one of three stories in his book \"Sing Sing Nights.\"\n- For many years, Roger Angell wrote an annual Christmas poem for The New Yorker.\n- Roger Angell also wrote numerous works of fiction, non-fiction, and criticism.\n- Roger Angell wrote the 1988 book \"Season Ticket: A Baseball Companion,\" and his previous works included \"Five Seasons,\" \"Late Innings,\" and the New York Times best-seller \"The Summer Game.\"\n- The film \"The Mysterious Mr. Wong\" is based on Harry Stephen Keeler's 1928 short story \"The Strange Adventure of the Twelve Coins of Confucius.\"\n- Harry Stephen Keeler died on January 22, 1967.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a05e7002-74af-511e-854d-a8949803792c",
        "text": "Page: Roger Angell. Sentence: Roger Angell (born September 19, 1920) is an American essayist known for his writing on sports, especially baseball.\nPage: Roger Angell. Sentence: He has written numerous works of fiction, non-fiction, and criticism, and for many years wrote an annual Christmas poem for \"The New Yorker\".\nPage: Harry Stephen Keeler. Sentence: Harry Stephen Keeler (November 3, 1890 – January 22, 1967) was a prolific but little-known American author of mysteries and science fiction.\nPage: Season Ticket: A Baseball Companion. Sentence: Season Ticket: A Baseball Companion is a 1988 book written by Roger Angell, whose previous works include \"Five Seasons\", \"Late Innings\", and the New York Times best-seller, \"The Summer Game\".\nPage: The Mysterious Mr. Wong. Sentence: The film is based on Harry Stephen Keeler's 1928 short story \"The Strange Adventure of the Twelve Coins of Confucius\" one of three stories in Keeler's book \"Sing Sing Nights\".",
